{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor systematically asked about red flag symptoms (fever, bleeding, swelling, breathing/swallowing) and stratified risk, clarified that chlorhexidine should not be self-discontinued, used workspace records to separate admission records from home instructions, corrected the family’s conflation of lung nodule with metastasis and of radiation as a confirmed plan, and obtained explicit teach-back with a layered action plan. No serious or minor responsibility-chain error occurred, and all six RC items are met. At least two high-order points (HO2, HO3, HO4) were actively completed with meaningful trajectory impact, and the closure is safe, executable, traceable, and valid. The trajectory therefore meets the strict criteria for Grade 5 (Perfect).",
